1
00:00:00,660 --> 00:00:03,682
This is Cedar, our sample export project.

2
00:00:03,912 --> 00:00:06,969
Let’s follow one request from evidence to decision.

3
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:11,702
Cedar already has a CSV export spec.

4
00:00:11,932 --> 00:00:17,418
Socrates names its owner and lists the four fields in this saved OpenAI answer.

5
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:24,959
Open the citation and you can check those fields in the document, not just in the chat.

6
00:00:25,189 --> 00:00:27,833
Now we know exactly what the baseline says.

7
00:00:30,306 --> 00:00:36,612
Deep Research pulls together a longer view of the project with its sources and open questions.

8
00:00:36,842 --> 00:00:39,043
This saved report is research, though.

9
00:00:39,273 --> 00:00:41,694
It cannot turn a request into an approval.

10
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:45,266
The Truth Inbox shows what needs review.

11
00:00:45,496 --> 00:00:50,124
Change the view to see work assigned to you, or look back at resolved items.

12
00:00:50,354 --> 00:00:52,693
Let’s review the PDF request.

13
00:00:55,660 --> 00:01:01,027
The change packet shows the recorded wording on the left and the proposed wording on the right.

14
00:01:01,257 --> 00:01:04,870
The reviewer can check the source and what the change affects.

15
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:12,624
An authorized reviewer can accept the change here.

16
00:01:12,854 --> 00:01:15,397
Finding a document didn’t approve anything.

17
00:01:15,627 --> 00:01:18,780
After saving, the packet shows the approved wording.

18
00:01:22,660 --> 00:01:25,480
The approval has a record of who made it and when.

19
00:01:25,710 --> 00:01:28,574
Open the delivery trace to see what’s still missing.

20
00:01:28,804 --> 00:01:32,710
An accepted requirement is not evidence that the feature shipped.

21
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:39,344
Project Memory gives you another way into the same work.

22
00:01:39,574 --> 00:01:45,468
Start with the project, choose a change or a source, then follow the branch to its linked records.

23
00:01:50,611 --> 00:01:54,775
Select the document section to read its excerpt underneath the map.

24
00:01:55,005 --> 00:01:59,680
Open the passage and Orchestra takes you to that revision of the source.

25
00:01:59,910 --> 00:02:03,389
The source list still gives you the original document view.

26
00:02:04,434 --> 00:02:07,557
Back in Delivery, prepare the engineering task.

27
00:02:07,787 --> 00:02:16,566
The request is now precise: implement PDF export for Cedar without changing the existing CSV acceptance criteria.

28
00:02:17,660 --> 00:02:23,546
Agent Preflight gathers the relevant project context into a pack with a specific ID.

29
00:02:23,776 --> 00:02:27,800
It keeps approved scope separate from the questions that still need review.

30
00:02:32,660 --> 00:02:41,742
That’s the workflow: find what changed, check the source, make the decision, then hand the approved context to the people or agents doing the work.

31
00:02:45,660 --> 00:02:49,473
Start with one project and one decision that keeps coming up.

32
00:02:49,703 --> 00:02:52,237
Give the team a record they can return to.

33
00:02:53,660 --> 00:02:56,777
Orchestra. Product Brain for High Speed Teams.
